Stable sorts: the same BV tree and contours on every platform

dtCreateNavMeshData's BV tree (subdivide: compareItemX, compareItemY,
compareItemZ) and rcBuildContours' hole merging (mergeRegionHoles:
compareHoles, compareDiagDist) sort with the C library's qsort. qsort is not
stable, and glibc, macOS libSystem, the Windows UCRT and emscripten's musl
put items with equal keys in different orders; on a mesh laid out on a grid
the keys tie often, so the same input gave different BV trees and contour
merges, different mesh bytes, and a crowd on the mesh walked differently by
platform. The five calls use std::stable_sort with the same comparators: a
stable sort's result is determined by the comparator and the input order, so
it is the same everywhere. Where the keys do not tie nothing changes.
Upstream-worthy, not yet upstream.

Apply from upstream/recastnavigation: git apply -p1 ../../patches/0004-stable-sorts.patch

